  "worked_solution": "The osculating plane passes through the point $P$, which is at the tip of the vector $r(0).$ The vectors $T(0)$ and $N(0)$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, a parametric equation for the plane can be written as\n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(0)+s\\,T(0)+u\\,N(0),\\,s,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =\u27e80,\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u20610-\\operatorname{sin}\u20610,\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u20610+\\operatorname{sin}\u20610\u27e9=\u27e80,1,1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, a parametric equation for the osculating plane at the point $(0,1,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(0)+s\\,T(0)+u\\,N(0) \\\\  & =\u27e80,1,1\u27e9+s\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\u27e8-1,-1,1\u27e9+u\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\u27e80,-1,-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,1-\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{u\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1+\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{u\\sqrt{2}}{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
